  "desc": "A cached poster is decomposed into real red, green, and blue channel buffers. Deterministic horizontal bands displace and reconstruct those channels during hover bursts, producing chromatic tears rather than duplicated CSS text.",
  "seen": "Seen on: broadcast identities, electronic music releases, speculative-tech portfolios",
  "hint": "hover to corrupt the transmission or inject a burst",
  "prompt": "Build RGB Slices with the approved photo-cityNight image in the exact 200×150px rounded v4 frame at (86,28), using cover cropping. Preserve its three initial clipped strips at y=40/70/96 with heights 18/14/10, offsets -8/+8/-5 and unchanged separator SVGs. Live native slices project original sorted bands 0/4/9 with the original seeded shifts, jitter, channel separation, 860ms envelope, scan focus and automatic cadence. Full retains all ten original bands and uses approved photo-archGrid photography. Keep retina native backing pixels and both Unsplash credits/licence comments. Shell actions inject and clear a burst; Up/Down, Home, Space/Enter and Escape retain the original input model. Use the v4 neutral palette and self-hosted Geist/Geist Mono. Keep a 240×168 hero plane with exact native artwork and a separate complete 400×400 full composition with a readable scroll camera. Prefix every class with rootClass. Keep controls in the shell, support native keys and touch scrolling, preserve source timing and datasets, freeze work during independent caller/viewport holds, and clean up frames, observers, capture and font/image work. Reduced motion keeps an intentional still with interruptible 150ms opacity feedback. Portable exports resolve both fonts and licensed assets without network access.\n\nKeep native vertical page scrolling available when the full viewport reaches its bounds, while retaining horizontal overscroll containment, deliberate camera panning and the original geometry, assets and complete model.",
